# `(Γ_p, ℓ(p))`-circles, `ℝP¹`-circles, `G̃` acting on `ℝP̃¹`, and the real angle

Target `T-bbs-rp1-circles` (`roadmap/roadmap.toml`; DEC-192: BBS's layer L2 lives in lean-gx;
wave W2 of `papers/bbs/REVIEW.md` §E). `papers/bbs/legacy/labeled/colI_v1.tex`. 0 `sorry`.

* **`bbsdef:circle_data_point_structure`** — `colI_v1.tex:766` — `GX.GammaLinkCircle`, with
  `ℓ(p)` (`GX.Link`), `T_p HS²` (`GX.TpHS`), `Γ_p` (`GX.GammaP`) and its action on `ℓ(p)`;
  `ℓ(p)` is a circle (`GX.isCircle_link`) and is itself a `(Γ_p, ℓ(p))`-circle
  (`GX.GammaLinkCircle.regular`). The sentence after it (l.770–771, no label) is proved too,
  under the double-cover reading of its "natural `ℝP¹`-structure" (SCOPE (e)):
  `GX.GammaLinkCircle.rp1_hasGroupoid`, `GX.GammaLinkCircle.rp1_compatible`.

> For every $p$ in $\HS^2$, let $\ell(p)$ the link of $p$, \textit{i.e.} the space of rays in
> $T_p\HS^2$. [...] Let $\Gamma_p$ be the \textit{pointwise} stabilizer in
> $\SO_0(1,2)\approx \op{PSL}(2, \R)$ of $p$, \textit{i.e.} the subgroup which preserves every
> point of the ray $p$ in $\R^{1,2}$. (l.762–764)
>
> A $(\Gamma_p, \ell(p))$-circle is the data of a point $p$ in $\HS^2$ and a
> $(\Gamma_p, \ell(p))$-structure on the circle. (l.767)
>
> Since $\HS^2$ is oriented, $\ell(p)$ admits a natural $\R\PP^1$-structure, and thus every
> $(\Gamma_p, \ell(p))$-circle admits a natural underlying $\R\PP^1$-structure. (l.770–771)

The prose of §3.3.1 that the Θ-half of `T-3p1-theorem-m` needs (no label; l.675–744):

> Let $G$ be the group $\operatorname{PSL}(2, \R)$ of projective transformations of $\R\PP^1$,
> and let $\tilde{G}$ be its universal covering: it is the group of projective transformations of
> $\widetilde{\R\PP^1}$. We have an exact sequence: [...] Let $\delta$ be the generator of the
> center $\Z$ such that for every $x$ in $\widetilde{\R\PP}^1$ the inequality $\delta x > x$
> holds. (l.678–685)

## Main declarations

* **`ℝP¹` and `G = PSL(2,ℝ)`.** `GX.RP1` is `ℝP¹ = P(ℝ²)`, represented by the circle: the line
  `ℝ z` is `z / z̄` (`GX.RP1.mk`; `GX.RP1.mk_eq_mk_iff`: same point iff same line;
  `GX.RP1.isQuotientMap_sq`). `PSL(2,ℝ)` is mathlib's `Matrix.ProjectiveSpecialLinearGroup`,
  acting projectively (`[g]·[z] = [g z]`, `GX.RP1.sl_smul_mk`); **analytic** in gx's sense
  (`GX.isAnalyticAction_rp1`: faithful and rigid); **centreless** (`GX.psl_center_eq_bot`).
* **`ℝP̃¹ = ℝ`**, covering `t ↦ [cos πt : sin πt]` (`GX.RP1.proj`, `GX.RP1.isCoveringMap_proj`),
  deck group `t ↦ t + n`; `ℝP̃¹/ℤ ≃ₜ ℝP¹` (`GX.RP1.addCircleHomeomorph`, l.685–686).
* **`G̃`** (`GX.GTilde`): the lifts to `ℝP̃¹` of the elements of `PSL(2,ℝ)`, a subgroup of the
  units of mathlib's `CircleDeg1Lift`; it acts on `ℝP̃¹` by increasing homeomorphisms commuting
  with `δ`. Every element of `SL(2,ℝ)` lifts, and every lift commutes with `t ↦ t + 1`
  (`GX.slDeg_eq_one`: `SL(2,ℝ)` is generated by squares). **The exact sequence
  `0 → ℤ → G̃ → G → 0`** (l.682): `GX.GTilde.zpow_delta_injective`, `GX.GTilde.ker_toPSL`,
  `GX.GTilde.toPSL_surjective`; **`δ`** with `δ x = x + 1 > x` (`GX.GTilde.delta_apply`), and
  **the centre of `G̃` is `⟨δ⟩`** (`GX.GTilde.center_eq_zpowers`).
* **The classification** (l.688–699): `GX.PSL2.IsElliptic`/`IsParabolic`/`IsHyperbolic` by the
  trace, `GX.PSL2.trichotomy`; elliptic elements of `G̃` act **freely and properly
  discontinuously** (`GX.GTilde.IsElliptic.zpow_apply_ne`,
  `GX.GTilde.IsElliptic.properlyDiscontinuousSMul`); **`g̃ = δᵏ g`**, `g` with a fixed point,
  `k` unique (`GX.GTilde.exists_delta_zpow_mul_of_not_isElliptic`,
  `GX.GTilde.delta_zpow_mul_unique`).
* **The real angle** of `f ∈ G̃`: `GX.GTilde.angle f = 2π τ(f)` (mathlib's translation number),
  a conjugacy invariant (`GX.GTilde.angle_conj`), `angle δ = 2π`, `angle (δᵏ g) = 2πk` when `g`
  has a fixed point (`GX.GTilde.angle_eq_of_delta_zpow_mul`).
* **`ℝP¹`-circles** (l.728–729): `[ChartedSpace RP1 L] [HasGroupoid L (gxGroupoid PSL(2,ℝ) RP1)]`
  with `GX.IsCircle L`. **The lifted holonomy** `GX.HasLiftedHolonomy L f` (l.729–737: a lift
  `D : ℝ → ℝP̃¹` of a developing map, increasing, `D (s + 1) = f (D s)`) **exists**
  (`GX.exists_hasLiftedHolonomy`, from gx's developing theorem) **and is unique up to
  conjugacy in `G̃`** (`GX.HasLiftedHolonomy.conj`). Hence **the real angle of an `ℝP¹`-circle**
  `GX.HasRealAngle L θ` is well defined (`GX.HasRealAngle.unique`, `GX.exists_hasRealAngle`),
  `≥ 0`, `> 0` when elliptic (`GX.HasRealAngle.pos_of_isElliptic`); the degree is `≥ 0`
  (`GX.HasLiftedHolonomy.deg_nonneg`, l.740). `ℝP¹` itself: holonomy `δ`, angle `2π`
  (`GX.hasRealAngle_rp1`).
* **The natural `ℝP¹`-structure of `ℓ(p)`** (l.770), read (SCOPE (e)) as the double covering
  `ℓ(p) = S(T_p HS²) → P(T_p HS²) ≅ ℝP¹` read through an oriented `θ : T_p HS² ≃ ℂ`
  (`GX.linkToRP1`, `GX.IsOrientedTangent`, `GX.exists_isOrientedTangent`), `Γ_p`-equivariant
  through `GX.gammaToSL` (`det = 1`, `GX.det_tangent`), independent of `θ`
  (`GX.linkToRP1_eq_smul`); `ℓ(p)` has lifted holonomy `δ²` and real angle `4π`
  (`GX.hasRealAngle_link`).
* **Change of model** along an equivariant map, for any `(G, X)`, `(H, Y)`:
  `GX.trans_symm_trans_mem_gxGroupoid`, `GX.hasGroupoid_comp_of_equivariant`.

